    "revised_section": [
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Note: There is substantial benefit to studying applications and ethics/fairness/trust/explainability in a curriculum alongside the methods and theory that they apply to, rather than covering ethics in a separate, dedicated class session. Whenever possible, study of these topics should be integrated alongside other modules, such as exploring how decision trees could be applied to a specific problem in environmental sustainability such as land use allocation, then assessing the social/environmental/ethical implications of doing so."
          }
        ],
